        "original_id": "633ce6b9-c441-523e-92bb-294fb52cf48d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mikhail Kozakov, Oleg Menshikov, Anatoly Ravikovich, Régis Wargnier, Sandrine Bonnaire, Sergei Bodrov Jr., Catherine Deneuve, Leonid Bronevoy, Inna Ulyanova\n- Films: The Pokrovsky Gate, East/West\n- Roles: actor, theatre director, singer, director\n\nFacts:\n- In 1982, Anatoly Ravikovich appeared in Mikhail Kozakov's comedy film The Pokrovsky Gate.\n- The Pokrovsky Gate was directed by Mikhail Kozakov and stars Oleg Menshikov, Leonid Bronevoy, and Inna Ulyanova.\n- Oleg Evgenyevich Menshikov was born on 8 November 1960 and is a Russian actor, theatre director, and occasional singer.\n- In 1999, East/West was released as an internationally co-produced film directed by Régis Wargnier.\n- East/West stars Sandrine Bonnaire as Marie, Oleg Menshikov as Alexei, Sergei Bodrov Jr. as Sasha, and Catherine Deneuve as Gabrielle.",
